# Kotlin code style (write + refactor)

**Parity doc:** `docs/CODE_AND_REFACTOR_STYLE.md`. **Refactor batches:** `docs/REFACTOR_GUIDE.md` Phases 0–7 + `chinese-listener-refactor.mdc`.

This repo follows the **same refactoring discipline** as `kotlin-mutliplatform-test`: pattern catalog, strict phases, audit, and **stdlib collection style** — adapted to single-module `:app` (see `ANDROID_PRACTICES.md`, not KMP source sets).

## Collections (non-negotiable)

`chinese-listener-kotlin-collections.mdc` applies. **No** imperative `for` / `while` / `do-while` in any Kotlin source (app + tests).

- SSOT matrix: `docs/REFACTOR_PLAYBOOK.md` §4
- Indexed scan / wrap helpers: `com.example.chineselistener.util.KotlinLoopReplacements` — extend there instead of adding loops

## Modern Kotlin (every change)

- `data class` + `copy` for state; `sealed interface` / `sealed class` for events, results, errors
- `val` over `var`; avoid `!!` — `requireNotNull` or early return
- Coroutines: `viewModelScope`, `StateFlow`, `update { }`; **no** `GlobalScope`
- Domain: pure functions + collection ops; **no** `android.*` or Compose in `domain`
- UDF: composables observe state and emit events only

## Patterns (when designing or refactoring)

Before introducing structure, pick names from `docs/PATTERNS_REFERENCE.md` (cite **PR-§*n*** in chat/audit):

- **Layers:** PR-§3 layered / clean / ports & adapters (`ui` → `presentation` → `domain` ← `data`)
- **Presentation:** UDF / MVVM-shaped — `StateFlow` + sealed events
- **Data rim:** Repository, DTO mapper, anti-corruption at API boundary
- **Behavioral:** Strategy, Command (events), Observer (`StateFlow`), Facade (composition root)

Do **not** introduce microservices, CQRS, or event sourcing without explicit approval (REFACTOR_GUIDE in-scope list).

## Refactor vs feature work

| Work | Required |
|------|----------|
| New feature code | This rule + `chinese-listener-architecture.mdc` + collection rule |
| Multi-file / style / structure | `chinese-listener-refactor.mdc` + REFACTOR_GUIDE Phases 0–7 + update `REFACTOR_AUDIT.md` |
| Rename-only | Still no new loops; run unit tests if behavior touched |

